loss":"kite/vulture"}],"gloss":"bright vulture"},{"surface":"ஆர்ப்பத்","parts":[{"text":"ஆர்ப்ப","lemma":"ārppa","gloss":"to screech"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"t","gloss":"glide"}],"gloss":"to screech"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தடிந்துமாறு","parts":[{"text":"தடிந்து","lemma":"taṭintu","gloss":"having cut down"},{"text":"மாறு","lemma":"māṟu","gloss":"opposing/returning"}],"gloss":"cutting down and opposing"},{"surface":"பெயர்த்தது","parts":[{"text":"பெயர்த்தது","lemma":"peyarttatu","gloss":"it retrieved/turned back"}],"gloss":"retrieved"},{"surface":"இக்","parts":[{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"this"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"k","gloss":"glide"}],"gloss":"this"},{"surface":"கருங்கை","parts":[{"text":"கருங்கை","lemma":"கருங்கை","gloss":"strong-handed"}],"gloss":"strong-handed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வாளே","parts":[{"text":"வாள்","lemma":"vāḷ","gloss":"sword"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"sword indeed"}]}],"literal":"Wild jasmine with sharp buds like a koel's beak, / a sparsely strung many-stranded garland, / having adorned to shine on his dark black tuft of hair, / containing hot roasted meat like tiger's eyes in a new clay bowl, / after drinking one or two times sitting in order, / as the tuṭi drummer wearing a foliage wreath arrived, / asking for the food of squeezed toddy, / they said, 'Accept this!' and praised him with toddy; / knowing that they extended to Karantai, in the battle, / to the bowmen who gathered the herds of many cows, / while curved-winged bright vultures screeched, / cutting down and opposing, it retrieved them, this strong-handed sword!","translation":"Adorning his dark black tuft of hair with a sparsely strung, many-stranded garland of wild jasmine whose sharp buds resemble a koel's beak, he sat in order and drank once or twice, eating hot roasted meat resembling tiger's eyes served in a new clay bowl. When the drummer wearing a wreath of foliage arrived and asked for the food of squeezed toddy, they said, 'Accept this!' and praised him with toddy. Knowing that the enemy had taken the cattle to the wide Karantai fields, in the battle against the bowmen who had gathered the herds of many cows, while curved-winged bright vultures screeched, this strong-handed sword cut down the enemies and retrieved the cattle!","modern":"குயிலின் அலகு போன்ற கூர்மையான அரும்புகளைக் கொண்ட அதிரல் மலர்களை நெருக்கமின்றித் தொடுத்த பல வடங்களைக் கொண்ட மாலையைத் தனது கரிய குடுமியில் அழகுபெறச் சூடி, புதிய அகல் பாத்திரத்தில் வைக்கப்பட்ட புலியின் கண் போன்ற சூடான இறைச்சியை, ஒன்று அல்லது இரண்டு முறை வரிசையாக அமர்ந்து உண்ட பின்னர், தழையினாலான மாலையை அணிந்த துடி முழக்கும் பாணன் வந்தான் என்று கூறி, அவன் பிழிந்த கள்ளையும் உணவையும் வேண்ட, 'இதனைப் பெற்றுக்கொள்வாயாக' என்று கூறி அவனுக்குக் கள்ளைக் கொடுத்து வாழ்த்தினர். பகைவர்கள் கரந்தைப் பூக்கள் நிறைந்த இடத்திற்குப் பசுக்களைக் கவர்ந்து சென்றதை அறிந்து, போரிலே பல பசுக்கூட்டங்களை வளைத்துக் கவர்ந்து சென்ற வில்லேந்திய வீரர்களை, வளைந்த சிறகுகளையுடைய பருந்துகள் ஆரவாரிக்கும்படி வெட்டி வீழ்த்தி, பகைமையை வென்று மீட்டது இந்த வலிய கையில் ஏந்திய வாளாகும்.","explanation":"The poet Avvaiyār praises the valor of a warrior and his sword in this Veṭci (cattle-raiding) poem, specifically under the theme of Uṇṭāṭṭu (the feast before or after a raid). The poem describes the warrior's preparation and celebration: he wears a garland of wild jasmine buds that look like koels' beaks on his dark hair, and feasts on hot roasted meat (which looks like tiger's eyes) and toddy. When a drummer arrives, he is generously offered toddy and food. The poem then shifts to the battlefield, where the warrior's strong-handed sword cut down the enemy bowmen who had raided their cattle and taken them to the Karantai fields, retrieving the herd while vultures circled and screeched above. The imagery of the tiger's eye for the meat and the koel's beak for the jasmine buds highlights the vivid natural observations of the classical poets.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.84],[0.93,1.01],[1.1,1.6],[1.6,2.0],[2.0,2.7],[2.7,3.0],[3.0,3.47],[3.47,3.7],[3.7,5.0],[5.0,5.2],[5.2,5.4],[5.4,6.0],[6.0,6.2],[6.2,7.5],[7.5,7.61],[7.73,8.3],[8.3,9.2],[9.2,9.8],[9.8,10.1],[10.1,10.3],[10.3,10.5],[11.3,11.73],[11.73,11.73],[11.73,12.3],[12.37,12.8],[12.8,12.8],[12.8,13.43],[13.8,14.2],[14.2,15.67],[15.67,15.73],[15.73,15.9],[15.9,16.2],[16.96,17.46],[17.46,17.66],[17.66,18.36],[18.36,18.76],[18.76,19.62],[20.1,20.22],[20.22,20.34],[20.34,20.94],[20.94,21.06],[21.06,23.25],[23.25,23.25],[23.25,24.56],[24.56,25.06],[25.06,25.06],[25.06,25.76],[25.76,26.06]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.5],[1.5,2.0],[2.0,2.7],[2.7,3.1],[3.1,3.77],[3.77,4.1],[4.1,5.3],[5.3,5.5],[5.5,5.8],[5.8,6.6],[6.6,7.35],[7.35,7.47],[7.47,7.47],[7.47,7.6],[7.6,8.4],[8.8,10.2],[10.2,10.38],[10.38,11.1],[11.1,12.2],[12.2,12.5],[12.5,12.6],[12.6,12.9],[12.9,12.9],[12.9,14.4],[14.4,14.7],[14.7,14.8],[14.8,16.1],[16.1,16.3],[16.38,16.8],[16.8,17.1],[18.04,18.64],[18.72,18.79],[18.79,19.54],[19.54,20.04],[20.04,21.04],[21.04,21.54],[21.54,21.84],[21.84,22.54],[22.54,22.54],[22.54,24.59],[24.59,24.59],[24.59,26.04],[26.04,26.74],[26.74,26.74],[26.74,27.34],[27.74,27.84]]},"sync":[[["குயில்வாய்","koel's beak"]],[["அன்ன","like"]],[["கூர்முகை","sharp bud"]],[["அதிரல்","wild jasmine"]],[["பயிலாது","sparsely"]],[["அல்கிய","strung"]],[["பல்காழ்","many-stranded"]],[["மாலை","garland"]],[["மையிரும்","dark black"]],[["பித்தை","tuft of hair"]],[["பொலியச்","to shine"]],[["சூட்டிப்","having adorned"]],[["புத்தகல்","new clay bowl"]],[["கொண்ட","containing"]],[["புலிக்கண்","tiger's eye"]],[["வெப்பர்","hot roasted meat"]],[["ஒன்றுஇரு","one or two"]],[["முறையிருந்து","sitting in turns"]],[["உண்ட","drunk"]],[["பின்றை","afterwards"]],[["உவலைக்","foliage"]],[["கண்ணித்","wreath"]],[["துடியன்","tuṭi drummer"]],[["வந்தெனப்","as he came"]],[["பிழிமகிழ்","squeezed toddy"]],[["வல்சி","food/drink"]],[["வேண்ட","asking for"]],[["மற்றிது","but this"]],[["கொள்ளாய்","accept this"]],[["என்ப","they say"]],[["கள்ளின்","with toddy"]